<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Caseros</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1852">1852</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/platine-war">Platine War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Caseros was fought on 3 February 1852 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> between the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-manuel-de-rosas">Juan Manuel de Rosas</a> and a coalition led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justo-jose-de-urquiza">Justo José de Urquiza</a>, governor of Entre Ríos, backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a>. Urquiza's victory ended Rosas's long rule and sent him into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, opening the way to the Argentine Constitution of 1853.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-caseros.jpg" alt="Battle of Caseros" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlo Penuti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalla_de_Caseros,_Litografia_de_Carlo_Penuti,_ca._1852.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
